en doubleton of clubs.\n\n"],["pg",""],["nt","\nThe mathematics of all of these possibilities favours cashing the top honours. That is, cashing the @CA and @CK is slightly more likely to work than taking the second round finesse."],["pg",""],["nt","\nA famous bridge saying can be used to help you remember this play. \"8 ever, 9 never\" means that if North and South have 8 cards in a suit missing only the Queen, it is correct to finesse for the Queen. With 9 cards between the 2 hands, as above, it is correct to play for the drop."],["",""]]}}